			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4156146">
									

<p>Don't describe an object as a subset of the scp designation (SCP-Z-X, where X is the subset) paragraphs after introducing the object. 4580-4 is a tree. Tell me it's a tree when you introduce 4580-4, not ages after.</p>
<p>Straight-up: the Foundation wouldn't exchange Foundation secrets for secrets. If there is ever a breach, the Foundation would have just handed whoever reached this object the secrets of the Foundation. The Foundation would either dictate terms or, if possible, negotiate for some precious commodity. This isn't an appeal to canon, just good sense. If I have a ton of cash and a lot of dangerous secrets, I'll trade in cash, not secrets. If I'm dirt poor, then and only then do you find out what happened at Band Camp.</p>

